### Weather Images API
# Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension and Visual Studio / Rider .http support.
# Flow: POST /api/jobs -> poll GET /api/jobs/{id} until status = "completed" -> open the image links.

@baseUrl = https://weather-func-bqurxt3tu2lka.kindhill-bfd226d6.italynorth.azurecontainerapps.io
# Local: func start in ./src
# @baseUrl = http://localhost:7071

### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Ping

### Start a new image job -> 202 Accepted { jobId, statusUrl }
# @name startJob
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/jobs

### Job status: "queued" -> "processing" (imagesCompleted/stationCount) -> "completed" with public blob links in "images"
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/jobs/{{startJob.response.body.jobId}}

### Fetch one generated image (copy a link from "images" above), e.g.
# GET https://<storage-account>.blob.core.windows.net/images/<jobId>/<stationId>.jpg

### Unknown job id -> 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/jobs/00000000000000000000000000000000
